e", "context": "Team Trees frames YouTuber culture as a powerful force for social change, showcasing the potential for digital influencers to impact environmental policies."}], "places": [{"name": "San Diego, USA", "role": "Campaign Launch"}, {"name": "Nebraska, USA", "role": "Major Tree Planting Site"}, {"name": "Los Angeles, USA", "role": "Influencer Hub"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Team Trees", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "team-trees"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q72904799", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Team_Trees"], "tags": ["environmental organization", "Development Banks & Aid Agencies", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Team Trees contributed to the historical record of the Contemporary period. Key lasting impacts include: Shaped institutional landscape and community development. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Team Trees significantly impacted environmental activism by raising substantial funds for tree planting, mobilizing millions to participate in conservation efforts, and inspiring subsequent campaigns.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-17T12:55:48Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29581803977", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Team Trees is a collaborative fundraiser that raised 20 million U.S. dollars before the start of 2020 to plant 20 million trees. The initiative was started by American YouTubers MrBeast and Mark Rober, and was mostly supported by YouTubers. All donations go to the Arbor Day Foundation, a tree planting organization that pledges to plant one tree for every U.S. dollar donated. The Arbor Day Foundation began planting in January 2020 with plans to end "no later than December 2022". It is estimated that 23 million trees would take up 210 km2 (81 sq mi) of land, absorb around 1.6 million tons of carbon and remove 116 thousand tons of pollutants from the atmosphere.", "newValue": "Team Trees emerged in October 2019 as a groundbreaking environmental initiative, spearheaded by prominent American YouTubers MrBeast (Jimmy Donaldson) and Mark Rober, aiming to address the escalating global crisis of deforestation. The campaign's significance lies in its capacity to mobilize a diverse audience across digital platforms, transcending traditional fundraising methods and engaging millions in the environmental movement. By leveraging the power of social media, Team Trees exemplifies a contemporary response to climate change, emphasizing the role of individuals and communities in global ecological efforts.

The initiative set an ambitious goal: to raise $20 million for the Arbor Day Foundation to plant 20 million trees. By the end of 2019, Team Trees had surpassed its target, with donations pouring in from YouTubers and fans alike, showcasing the collective power of grassroots activism. The Arbor Day Foundation commenced tree planting operations in January 2020, with a commitment to complete the project by December 2022. This endeavor not only aimed to contribute to reforestation efforts but also sought to raise awareness about environmental conservation, with each dollar donated translating directly into a tree planted.

